ions were  voluntary  while a subsidiary of sinopharm didn't  say if it informed those vaccinated of  potential risks  in august russia made headlines  after having tested sputnik v on 76  people  the ministry of health registered the  vaccine russia has said the registration  is conditional and published positive  data from early clinical trials of the  shot  the vaccine while still being in trials  it is already approved for  a limited purpose in the west you have  to go through  three phases on tens of thousands of  people in order to test that many people  western drug makers have looked abroad  for volunteers  and russia and china are doing the same  china  has appeared to bring the virus under  control  within its own borders in order to test  for efficacy of a vaccine  scientists need countries where the  virus is still circulating and  preferably in countries where  the case count is still high china has  started up trials in a lot of developing  countries  as well as some wealthier states even  bahrain's crown prince is among the  participants  but russia and china's vaccines haven't  been shown to be effective  if they're handed out widely and turn  out not to work this could accelerate  the spread of the virus  these partnerships could leave countries  that are struggling to contain the virus  in a financially vulnerable position  remember pakistan in august a chinese  state drug maker made one of the first  deals with the country to test vaccines  there  but the financial terms haven't been  worked out raising questions about how  pakistan will repay  china and it's not a trivial question  because islamabad is already financially  saddled to china through beijing's  huge infrastructure building program  called the belt and road initiative  over the next 20 years pakistan will  have to pay back china 40 billion  dollars  china says islamabad owes far less for  projects that are in the works  for china vaccine diplomacy might not  just give it financial leverage  but also a political one the chinese  government and at least one private drug  maker have offered vaccines to some of  its neighbors in the south china sea  a region where china has clashed with  other countries over its territorial  claims  beijing has talked about garnering  support from countries  on territorial claims in the south china  sea in the same statements that it also  talks about deepening  vaccine-related collaboration beijing  has also decided to take a larger  leadership role by joining the world  health organization's kovacs initiative  a major effort to distribute coven 19  vaccines to poorer countries  a project the u.s has rejected  although russia doesn't have china's  deep pockets its sputnik v vaccine could  also  help it make new friends and expand its  influence  in terms of the way moscow is  approaching its  export strategy it is looking at the  middle east where it has key  trade and energy partners is looking at  brazil a huge  growing economy and it is looking at  india and  developing countries in asia it is a  major  signpost to show that russia is back on  the global stage and not just in its  traditional  expertise areas like military exports  like  energy oil and gas but also in  technology  many people still believe that china is  to blame for this global health crisis  so if china can show that it can help  stop spread the virus with a vaccine  that might ease perceptions of  china being a kind of bad actor although  many in the west note the effectiveness  of their shots remains to be proven  beijing and moscow are pushing to get a  head start in the global vaccine race  vying for prestige deals and sway
 

